From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:19:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] confirm mini queue scans and continue short
 nonterminal pages

GitHub returned in_progress page2 total_count23 with four of five rows and rel=next; continuing returned eleven later rows. Short does not mean exhausted. Stop on empty or a short page reaching total_count; without totals continue to empty. Confirm all states with a second bounded scan and union IDs to recover offset shifts, retaining one jobs read per run and existing cap/fail-open policy. This is bounded reconciliation, not snapshot completeness.

Proof: both short-page and offset-shift regression tests RED (assert True is False) before their respective fixes; canonical tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py GREEN 23 passed, 0 skipped. Live raw responses retained on task t_01a1d763a64978cd; no actual eligible live omission claimed, no mini writes.
---
 scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py        | 22 +++++----
 tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py b/scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py
index c661bed372..00dbb04595 100644
--- a/scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py
